* =====================================================================================================
* load_switches__bq25180.lib  --  TI BQ25180 power path, as the VSYS source seen by the main-board load switches
* =====================================================================================================
* Part      : Texas Instruments BQ25180YBGR (base board U1, DSBGA-8)
* Datasheet : https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/bq25180.pdf  SLUSE99C (Sept 2021, revised Jan 2023)
* Register settings used (docs/architecture.md 6.5, docs/firmware.md 12.x): SYS_REG 0x40 = 4.5 V on USB,
*   TMR_ILIM ILIM code 500 mA (475 mA typ), CHARGECTRL1 BATOCP 1.5 A, BUVLO 3.0 V.
* Two sub-circuits, chosen by the test:
*   LSW_BQ25180_BAT  battery only (no VBUS): cell source vbat (the battery terminal voltage before the event)
*                    -> rpack (cell + PCM + leads, NOT a BQ25180 parameter; given by the test)
*                    -> BATFET RON_BAT (Table 7.5: 55 mOhm typ, 90 mOhm max) -> SYS.  Fully on, linear.
*   LSW_BQ25180_USB  VBUS present: input FET from IN to SYS regulated to min(VSYS_REG, VBUS) with output
*                    resistance RON_IN (Table 7.5: 270 mOhm typ, 470 mOhm max; also used in regulation, which
*                    makes the modelled droop pessimistic) and current limit ILIM (500 mA code: 450 / 475 /
*                    498 mA min/typ/max) through the XSPICE "ilimit" block.  The block may also SINK (through
*                    RON_IN): physically SYS never rises above the regulation target in these scenarios, but a
*                    source-only block lets Newton park SYS at absurd voltages, so sinking is allowed.
*                    VSYS_REG accuracy +-2 % (Table 7.5 VSYS_REG_ACCURACY) -> param vsysreg.
*                    Battery supplement (Table 7.5 VBSUP1 = 40 mV: battery feeds SYS when VSYS < VBAT - 40 mV):
*                    diode with ~40 mV at ~10 mA (IS 3.4e-16, N 0.05) in series with RON_BAT and rpack.
* NOT modelled: BATOCP / BUVLO / ILIM-interrupt / thermal trips (the tests compare currents and voltages against
*   those thresholds instead), the BUVLO gate on supplement mode (SLUSE99C 8.3.3: no supplement while VBAT <
*   VBUVLO; the D_SUP diode always conducts, so a test models a cell below BUVLO with vbat=0), input UVLO/OVP, VINDPM, regulation-loop dynamics, the charge current (assumed to
*   give way instantly to the system load, DPPM), the 25 Ohm SYS pull-down (ship/shutdown only).
* Pins: SYS GND.
* =====================================================================================================

.subckt LSW_BQ25180_BAT SYS GND params: vbat=3.7 rpack=0.25 ronbat=55m
V_BAT    VCELL GND {vbat}
R_PACK   VCELL BAT {rpack}
R_BATFET BAT SYS {ronbat}
.ends LSW_BQ25180_BAT

.subckt LSW_BQ25180_USB SYS GND params: vbus=5.0 vsysreg=4.5 ronin=0.27 ilim=0.475 vbat=3.7 rpack=0.25 ronbat=55m
V_BUS    VBUS GND {vbus}
V_REF    VREG GND {min(vsysreg, vbus)}
a_INFET  VREG VBUS GND SYS lsw_bq_infet
.model lsw_bq_infet ilimit(in_offset=0 gain=1 r_out_source={ronin} r_out_sink={ronin} i_limit_source={ilim}
+        i_limit_sink=10 v_pwr_range=0.01 i_source_range=1e-2 i_sink_range=1e-2 r_out_domain=1e-3)
V_BAT    VCELL GND {vbat}
R_PACK   VCELL BAT {rpack}
D_SUP    BAT BSUP lsw_bq_sup
.model lsw_bq_sup d (is=3.4e-16 n=0.05 xti=0 eg=0)
R_BATFET BSUP SYS {ronbat}
.ends LSW_BQ25180_USB
